# install — how bits land
File: install/docs/SURFACE.oot

How the toolchain lands on a machine. Git tags are the
version (RFC-0006). Ships `install.sh` plus apt, dnf, and
pacman recipes. winget is deferred.

This repo is `openOODA/install`. It is not the
`ooda install` subcommand.

The public URL `https://openooda.org/install.sh` redirects
to this repo's `install.sh` on GitHub `main`.

Installs to `~/.openooda/`. Adds `~/.openooda/bin` to PATH.

## Surface

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `install.sh` | One-line installer. Idempotent. |
| `apt/` | Debian package |
| `dnf/` | Fedora and RHEL spec |
| `pacman/` | Arch PKGBUILD |
| `docs/INSTALL.md` | Install paths and flags |

Flags: `OPENOODA_DRY_RUN=1`, `NO_COLOR=1`,
`OPENOODA_HOME=…`.

Binaries: ooda, oodac, liboodar.a, opm, ooda-lsp, ooda-mcp.
std is a git clone under `~/.openooda/std`.
